description:
In pkix-profiles/src/lib.rs:355-356, the test web_pki_policy_san_field_is_true builds:
  let mut policy = pkix_path::ValidationPolicy::new(NOW);
  policy.require_subject_alt_name = true;
but then calls validate_path with `&web_pki_policy(NOW)` (line 370), not with `&policy`. The two lines that construct and mutate `policy` are dead — they have no effect on what the test exercises.

Fix: remove lines 355-356 and their associated misleading comment block (lines 351-364), which was written as if the test was going to use the custom policy but doesn't.

The test still has value after the removal — it checks that web_pki_policy sets require_subject_alt_name=true (line 347-350) and that a conforming cert passes (lines 365-371).
